{"parentUuid":"ed6f58be-dcfe-486e-8321-e287c5295176","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01GyHuqFRVBY9EeNQ9zbMKQ6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right — sorry, sloppy framing. Codex is registered the same way as Claude Code (`agent.Register(agent.AgentNameCodex, NewCodexAgent)` in `codex.go:21`), as a built-in agent compiled into the binary. The \"external\" path (the `agent/external` plugin protocol with `CapabilityDeclarer` + `TranscriptCompactor`) is separate, and Codex doesn't go through it. My earlier \"external agent\" wording was wrong.\n\nThe right way to describe what's special about Codex here is **hook coverage**, not packaging:\n\n| Agent | UserPromptSubmit | PostToolUse-equivalent | Stop |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Claude Code | ✅ | ✅ (PostToolUse → SaveStep) | ✅ |\n| Codex | ✅ | ❌ (only `pre-tool-use`, which is a no-op for lifecycle) | ✅ |\n\nThat's the actual fork in the data flow:\n\n- **Claude Code** populates `state.FilesTouched` incrementally during the turn via PostToolUse → SaveStep. By the time PostCommit fires, `state.FilesTouched` is the accurate per-tool-use list.\n- **Codex** never fires a per-tool-use lifecycle event (`agent/codex/lifecycle.go`: only `session-start`, `user-prompt-submit`, `stop`, and `pre-tool-use` which is explicitly returned as `nil` event). So `state.FilesTouched` stays empty through the whole turn.\n\nThis matters at PostCommit:\n\n```go\n// resolveFilesTouched (manual_commit_hooks.go:1779 in v0.5.6)\nif len(state.FilesTouched) > 0 {\n    return copy(state.FilesTouched)\n}\nreturn s.extractModifiedFilesFromLiveTranscript(ctx, state, state.CheckpointTranscriptStart)\n```\n\nFor Claude Code: returns `state.FilesTouched` (the actual files for this turn).\nFor Codex: empty → fallback parses **the entire Codex JSONL** from `state.CheckpointTranscriptStart` (which is 0 on the first commit) and returns every file mentioned in `apply_patch` calls — including any scratch files like the `.claude/worktrees/login-copy-code/...` paths visible in `prompt_attributions[1].user_added_per_file`.\n\nFrom there the bug chain is the same as before:\n\n1. First condense writes 42c322 with start=0, advances `state.CheckpointTranscriptStart` to 268.\n2. Carry-forward check: `filesTouchedBefore` = [yml, .claude/worktrees/...], committed = {yml}, remaining = [.claude/worktrees/...] → non-empty.\n3. `carryForwardToNewShadowBranch` runs → `state.CheckpointTranscriptStart = 0`, `state.CompactTranscriptStart = 0`, `state.PromptAttributions = nil` (matches what we see in 1bcdc44's metadata).\n4. Second condense reads `state.CheckpointTranscriptStart = 0`, writes 1bcdc44 with start=0.\n\nSo the trigger is **\"built-in agent without a per-tool-use hook + any uncommitted file the agent touched\"** — which is the common case for Codex sessions. Same root cause, just badly named upstream by me.\n\nPR #1120 is still unrelated — different function, different inconsistency direction."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_read_input_tokens":234850,"output_tokens":2739,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":2739,"cache_read_input_tokens":234850,"cache_creation_input_tokens":273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoQbiWfGU7PMvTEYesrp","type":"assistant","uuid":"378d5301-1af0-4365-9998-e7d2853c6850","timestamp":"2026-05-07T15:00:37.324Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b1ed7d58-eb6b-498c-931f-1f6f207e13c3","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"main"}
