{"parentUuid":"ec46c819-4fc1-450c-b025-bfc9b88f349d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Fk3RFzjyV1aakxvisb4GqW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary of audit + adaptations\n\n**E2E suite findings.** Only one Codex-specific E2E test exists (`e2e/tests/codex_resume_test.go`), and it's about resume behavior. The `ForEachAgent` tests that exercise the bug shape (`TestRapidSequentialCommits`, `TestAgentCommitsMidTurnUserCommitsRemainder`, `TestUserSplitsAgentChanges`, `TestSplitModificationsToExistingFiles`, `TestPartialStaging`) already run for Codex and assert checkpoint trailers + distinctness, but **none assert `checkpoint_transcript_start` advancement** — the exact field that surfaced the original bug. I didn't add a new E2E that requires real Codex API calls (cost), but I added what's needed so future work can:\n\n- **`SessionMetadata.CheckpointTranscriptStart`** is now exposed on the e2e testutil struct (`e2e/testutil/metadata.go`). Future tests can read `ReadSessionMetadata(...).CheckpointTranscriptStart` and assert it advances across same-session checkpoints.\n\n**Integration test.** I added two integration tests in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/codex_post_tool_use_test.go` that lock in the wiring without API calls:\n\n1. **`TestCodexPostToolUse_PopulatesFilesTouched`** — pre-creates a Codex session state, fires a `PostToolUse` hook with an `apply_patch` envelope containing `Add`/`Update`/`Delete` entries, verifies all three paths land in `state.FilesTouched`. This is the regression guard: if the codex parser, `agent.ToolUse` event, dispatcher case, or `RecordFilesTouched` regresses, this test fails.\n2. **`TestCodexPostToolUse_NonMutatingToolIsNoop`** — fires `PostToolUse` for a `shell` tool. Verifies state is unchanged. Without this filter, every shell call would churn state and risk overwriting genuine file accounting.\n\n**New test infrastructure:**\n- `CodexHookRunner` (with `SimulateCodexPostToolUseApplyPatch` and direct `runCodexHook`) added to `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/hooks.go`, mirroring `GeminiHookRunner`. Future Codex hook tests can reuse it.\n\n**Updated existing test:**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/setup_codex_hooks_test.go` already updated in the prior commit to assert the `entire hooks codex post-tool-use` command appears in `.codex/hooks.json` after `enable --agent codex`.\n\nBoth new tests pass:\n\n```\n--- PASS: TestCodexPostToolUse_PopulatesFilesTouched (0.50s)\n--- PASS: TestCodexPostToolUse_NonMutatingToolIsNoop (0.50s)\n```\n\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all green (lint 0 issues, 58 vogon canary tests + 4 external-agent E2E tests all passing).\n\nI deliberately didn't extend `TestRapidSequentialCommits` or similar `ForEachAgent` tests with a transcript-start advancement assertion — those run against real agent APIs and the assertion semantics depend on whether other agents (Claude, Gemini, etc.) advance the offset reliably under the same scenarios. That's a separate investigation rather than something to bundle here. The struct field is in place for whoever does that work."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":115,"cache_read_input_tokens":453870,"output_tokens":1199,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":115,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1199,"cache_read_input_tokens":453870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":115,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":115},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoYyPedwWRbqg1V9jnxe","type":"assistant","uuid":"1060aa32-2e12-46e3-bc62-bc7ce5e9dcff","timestamp":"2026-05-07T16:50:04.752Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Wo