{"parentUuid":"7f267883-fa0c-4f92-ad59-9c59ff139ace","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XSY7KAAFQQx7vbWgJ8FzbC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0116t1zCKCoN1tPssf1RCjgx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nTrack Codex apply_patch file changes via PostToolUse\n\nCodex (post-#18391, 2026-04-21) emits PostToolUse hooks for every\napply_patch invocation with the patch envelope in tool_input.command.\nWe now install a fourth hook entry pointing at `entire hooks codex\npost-tool-use`, parse the canonical Codex envelope (\"*** Add File:\",\n\"*** Update File:\", \"*** Delete File:\"), and emit an agent.ToolUse\nevent so handleLifecycleToolUse can merge the paths into FilesTouched.\n\nThe parser filters by tool_name, accepting \"apply_patch\" plus the\n\"Write\" and \"Edit\" matcher aliases Codex registers for compatibility\nwith Claude-style hook configs (see codex-rs/core/src/tools/hook_names\n.rs). Non-mutating tools (shell, MCP) produce a nil event and skip the\ndispatcher.\n\nclassifyApplyPatchPaths lives next to the existing\nextractFilesFromApplyPatch and routes Add → NewFiles, Update →\nModifiedFiles, Delete → DeletedFiles. Add wins over Update on path\nconflicts so consumers can reason about agent intent rather than just\n\"file changed\".\n\nThis fixes the bug where two checkpoints in the same Codex session\nboth record checkpoint_transcript_start = 0: state.FilesTouched is now\naccurate at PostCommit time, filesWithRemainingAgentChanges no longer\nsees scratch files as remaining, and carryForwardToNewShadowBranch\nstops firing spuriously and zeroing the offset.\n\nOlder Codex versions silently won't fire PostToolUse — same fail-mode\nas today's behavior, no regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit Codex wiring"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":